{% comment %}
  Email sign-up row for a course page, passed the course's `signup` block as
  `signup`. It renders nothing until both `action` (the URL the email is POSTed
  to) and `field` (the name of the form field carrying the email) are set, so an
  unconfigured course shows no box. For a Google Form with one short-answer
  question: action = https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/<FORM_ID>/formResponse,
  field = entry.<NUMBER> (the id shown by the form's "Get pre-filled link").
  Without JavaScript the browser posts to `action` and lands on the backend's
  own confirmation page; with it, assets/js/course-signup.js submits in place
  and shows the outcome in the status line. The input and button reuse the
  theme's newsletter styles; the row layout is in _sass/_base.scss.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign signup = include.signup %}
{% assign signup_action = signup.action | default: '' | strip %}
{% assign signup_field = signup.field | default: '' | strip %}
{% if signup_action != '' and signup_field != '' %}
  <form class="course-signup" action="{{ signup_action }}" method="post">
    <label class="course-signup-label" for="course-signup-email">
      <i class="ti ti-mail" aria-hidden="true"></i>
      {{- signup.text | default: 'Get course announcements by email' -}}
    </label>
    <input
      id="course-signup-email"
      class="newsletter-form-input"
      type="email"
      name="{{ signup_field }}"
      placeholder="{{ signup.placeholder | default: 'you@example.com' }}"
      autocomplete="email"
      required
    >
    <button type="submit" class="newsletter-form-button">
      {{- signup.button | default: 'Sign up' -}}
    </button>
    <p class="course-signup-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
  </form>
{% endif %}
